1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,200
Somebody on your team just found a problem with your product.

2
00:00:04,300 --> 00:00:06,500
Normally that becomes a vague message in Slack.

3
00:00:06,600 --> 00:00:08,500
This is the alternative.

4
00:00:08,600 --> 00:00:13,100
They point at the part of the page they mean.
Whatever they hover is outlined.

5
00:00:13,200 --> 00:00:16,200
There is no guesswork about what is being reported.

6
00:00:16,300 --> 00:00:19,300
Clicking locks it, and the outline stays.

7
00:00:19,400 --> 00:00:22,800
So they can see exactly what they are describing
while they describe it.

8
00:00:22,900 --> 00:00:26,100
Picked the wrong thing? Choose another.
What they wrote is kept.

9
00:00:26,200 --> 00:00:29,000
Their words survive the change of target.

10
00:00:29,100 --> 00:00:33,800
A category, and a way to reach them, because a report
you cannot follow up on is a report you cannot act on.

11
00:00:33,900 --> 00:00:36,400
The element, its position in the page, the surrounding
text, all of it goes with the words.

12
00:00:36,500 --> 00:00:37,300
Now it is something you can work from.
